  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Saturday)\nIssued at 1130 AM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nStrong high pressure remains in place Sunday with temperatures again \napproaching 80 F across the area along with light southeast winds. \nThe upper level high will shift eastwards a bit Monday and \nespecially Tuesday as a system moves by to the north of the area. \nAlthough the better dynamics and moisture will remain to the west of \nthe area, ensemble guidance hints at some shower potential on \nTuesday. Increased pops to mentionable for most of northeast OK on \nTuesday morning to cover this possibility, though any impacts \nwould likely be minimal. \n\nWarmer and dry weather resumes for the mid to late week period as \nanother deep trough settles into the west with strong ridging \ntowards the Great Lakes. The forecast area will sit in between these \nsystems, but closer to the ridge, with mild southerly flow pushing \nhighs back close to 80 F. The entire pattern becomes more \nprogressive towards next weekend with a fairly good ensemble signal \nto move the western trough into the region. Presumably this would \nmean cooler and wetter conditions return at that time, but details \nare scarce given the long range.",
